In the first step towards implementing the recently proposed Alchemist
class, I have made an "advanced alchemy" patch which includes:

* Dylan's litmus patch
* My gem/acid alchemy patch
* Nephi's colour-based alchemy patch
* My brewing patch

Plus I have added a new skill of "alchemy" which affects your chances
of making potions successfully. The probability of success, as a
percentage, is now given by:

chance = 30 + P_SKILL(P_ALCHEMY) * 10 + ACURR(A_INT) + ACURR(A_DEX)

which means that a starting out Caveman has about a 40-50% chance of
success and cannot improve, whereas a starting out Wizard has about 70%
which can improve to 90% (P_SKILLED).
This may need a little tweaking for balance.

The patch can be found at:
http://www.cse.unsw.edu.au/~malcolmr/nethack/3.4.3/alchemy.diff

